        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: обязанность",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обязанность (obyázannost) — \"a duty, a responsibility\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В мои обязанности входит работа с клиентами. V moí obyázannosti vkhódit rabóta s kliyéntami. My duties include working with clients."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Входить в обязанности — to be part of one’s duties."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обязанность (obyázannost) is built on обязать \"to oblige\", made of о- and вязать \"to tie, to bind\", from Proto-Slavic vęzati: a duty is what binds you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
